# This lane's history is REBUILT on every publish: the snapshot is squashed from the private tree, so a
# history occurrence's key depends on the commit that landed it — including the baseline commit itself.
# A history baseline here churns by construction and cannot converge (measured: v3 and v4 each died at the
# post-commit control with one NEW allowed-history key nobody approved). Scope for THIS lane: tree only.
# This narrows what the allow-marker control COMPARES, never what the gate SCANS: the gate still scans the
# full history for leaks, and a marker silencing a private-overlay match still fails. See SANITISATION.md,
# "Allow-control scope on a rebuilt lane", and the SCOPE note in checks/verify-allowed-hits.sh.
tree
